      "title": "Secret Store TLS Handshake Failures Due to Expired Certs or Firewall Blocking",
      "content_summary": "Addresses service unresponsiveness and timeouts in Secret Store caused by TLS handshake errors, specifically focusing on expired certificates and firewall misconfigurations.",
      "content_body": "When Secret Store requests hang or return TLS handshake errors, first verify the validity period of the server certificate. An expired certificate is a common root cause and requires immediate renewal via the PKI infrastructure. If the certificate is valid, check for firewall misconfigurations that might be blocking the specific TLS ports or terminating connections prematurely. Updating the relevant firewall rules to allow full bidirectional traffic on the configured ports typically resolves the timeout issues."
